"comparison": "Both Citi and Goldman Sachs disclose reserve and lending activities related to their financial assets, though Citi focuses on the specific ACL balance mechanics for 'other financial assets' while Goldman Sachs describes the revenue-generating lending activities within its Private Banking segment. Citi reports that the ACL reserve balance on other financial assets remained unchanged at $2.0 billion, driven by transfer risk from unremittable corporate dividends. In contrast, Goldman Sachs describes its private banking and lending activities as including loans secured by commercial and residential real estate and securities, which generate net interest income, but does not quantify the specific reserve balance for these assets in the same manner. Both disclosures fall under the Financial & Capital Resources taxonomy and concern the management and reserving of loan/financial asset portfolios.",
